Let's examine the origin/destination dispatch flow:

There are actions:

- load_origin_payload (requires origin_availability, origin_node, payload_unit, not origin_availability_locked)
- unload_origin_payload (requires candidate_prepared origin_availability, candidate_task_profile_linked, origin_availability_node_linked, origin_node_occupied, origin_payload_linked, not origin_availability_confirmed)
- activate_origin_node (requires candidate_prepared, candidate_task_profile_linked, origin_availability_node_linked, not origin_node_ready, not origin_node_occupied) -> effect origin_node_ready
- lock_origin_availability (requires candidate_prepared, candidate_operator_linked, origin_availability_node_linked, origin_node_ready, not origin_availability_locked) -> effect origin_availability_locked, origin_availability_confirmed
- assemble_transport_leg (requires origin_availability_locked, destination_availability_locked, origin_availability_node_linked, destination_availability_node_linked, origin_node_ready, destination_node_ready, origin_availability_confirmed, destination_availability_confirmed, transport_leg_available) -> effect transport_leg_assigned, leg linked, not transport_leg_available
- mark_origin_availability_dispatch_ready (requires origin_availability_locked, origin_availability_confirmed, transport_leg_assembled, transport_leg_loading_authorized, not dispatch_ready ?origin_availability) -> effect dispatch_ready ?origin_availability
- authorize_transport_leg_loading (requires transport_leg_assembled, origin_availability_locked, candidate_task_profile_linked ?origin_availability ?route_task_profile, not transport_leg_loading_authorized) -> effect transport_leg_loading_authorized
- execute_origin_dispatch (requires dispatch_allocated ?origin_availability, candidate_vehicle_linked ?origin_availability ?vehicle_unit, candidate_dispatch_slot_linked ?origin_availability ?dispatch_slot, not dispatched) -> effect dispatched, vehicle_available, dispatch_slot_available.

